DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ooppeennppaamm__ttttyyccoonnvv() function is a standard conversation function suit‐
     able for use on TTY devices.  It should be adequate for the needs of most
     text-based interactive programs.

     The ooppeennppaamm__ttttyyccoonnvv() function allows the application to specify a time‐
     out for user input by setting the global integer variable
     _o_p_e_n_p_a_m___t_t_y_c_o_n_v___t_i_m_e_o_u_t to the length of the timeout in seconds.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ooppeennppaamm__ttttyyccoonnvv() function returns one of the following values:

     [PAM_SUCCESS]       Success.

     [PAM_BUF_ERR]       Memory buffer error.

     [PAM_CONV_ERR]      Conversation failure.

     [PAM_SYSTEM_ERR]    System error.

